WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:04.387
When you save a fine-tuned Transformer, save the tokenizer with it.

00:00:04.387 --> 00:00:10.977
model.save_pretrained writes the model configuration and weights to the chosen directory.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:16.847
tokenizer.save_pretrained writes the vocabulary, tokenizer configuration, and special-token information.

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:24.382
Later, from_pretrained can load both objects from that same local folder.

00:00:24.382 --> 00:00:31.582
Keeping them together prevents a common deployment mistake: loading model weights with a tokenizer from a

00:00:31.582 --> 00:00:36.102
different checkpoint. If your model depends on a label mapping or custom configuration,

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:39.227
verify that those settings are saved as well.

00:00:39.227 --> 00:00:46.497
For reproducibility, also record the library versions, training data version, preprocessing steps,

00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:52.802
and evaluation results. A folder containing model files is not the full experiment.

00:00:52.802 --> 00:01:00.107
The goal is to make sure someone else—or you several months later—can load the same tokenizer-model pair and

00:01:00.107 --> 00:01:02.058
understand how it was produced.
